// band-sweep-run.bml — every Form band answers on fkwu, the one runtime: the sweep, in this process.
//
//   ./fkwu gate/band-sweep-run.bml </dev/null                                        every band the body keeps
//   printf '{"list":1}' | ./fkwu gate/band-sweep-run.bml                              name the workloads, run nothing
//   printf '{"match":"glass|landing"}' | ./fkwu gate/band-sweep-run.bml               the workloads whose label holds either word
//   printf '{"files":["form-stdlib/tests/boot-band.fk"]}' | ./fkwu gate/band-sweep-run.bml   one workload of exactly these files
//   printf '{"shard":2,"of":8}' | ./fkwu gate/band-sweep-run.bml                      every 8th workload, from the third: an operator starts eight of these
//
// Every leg is one cell_run call (docs/in-process-cells.md): the body begins no child to run a band and reads no stdout, stderr or
// exit back; a band's answer is the value of its record, a stop is the record's `stopped`, a leg that outlives its ceiling comes back
// stopped "deadline". Parallelism is sharding: the work is a list, and each shard reads the same tree.
//
// stdin is one JSON object, every key optional: list (1 names the workloads, with each one's staging, head pin and manifest
// row, and runs nothing), match (alternatives separated by |, each a substring of a workload's label), files (one workload of
// these files, in order: a path as given, else under form/), ceiling_s (a leg's deadline, 1800), shard and of (this sweep takes the
// workloads whose enumeration index is shard mod of). Run from the repository root. The enumeration, the legs, the judgment and
// the seal are form-stdlib/bml/band-sweep.bml.
//
// A request that does not read is refused by name and exit 1 before any leg (door-options.bml): malformed JSON, another JSON value, an
// unknown key, a key of the wrong kind or given twice. So is a `match` that selects no workload, a shard outside 0 up to (of - 1), and a
// form/band-verdicts.txt (or a band file) that does not read or is empty: its pins would be dropped silently and the sweep would still
// answer "every pin".
//
// Before the first leg the sweep (not the list) runs two gates and builds what is stale: the structural gate
// (gate/structural-gate-run.fk) must end 1, then gate/validation-start-run.fk must end 1, then the seed (runtime/fkwu-uni.c)
// and, on Darwin, the Metal carrier (form/native/metal/fk-metal-carrier.m) are built by `cc` when they are newer than their
// products: the C compiler is the one external tool the seed needs to be BUILT, begun by argv as the walk's own build is (the product
// is made beside itself and renamed over, never written into the live binary).
//
// Output: one line per workload in enumeration order, then the summary. The exit is 0 only when every workload held; a failed
// workload, a refused gate or a void reading (the tree moved while the sweep ran) ends in an error naming it.
// preflight-exec: forbidden
// preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk form-stdlib/bml/band-sweep.bml
section [form.bml] {
 bsw-request(bsw-doc(bsw-stdin()));
}
